  "verbalization": "Divaricataester C is implicated in the biological activity of SK-VLB through a series of molecular interactions involving the CMP-N-acetylneuraminate-beta-1,4-galactoside alpha-2,3-sialyltransferase enzyme. This enzyme is a target of multiple compounds, including (3aR,6S,6aR)-3,6-bis(3,4,5-trimethoxyphenyl)-1,3,3a,4,6,6a-hexahydrofuro[3,4-c]furan and (1S,2R,7R,9S,10S)-6-acetyl-6'-methoxy-1'-methylspiro[4-oxa-12-azatricyclo[7.2.1.02,7]dodec-5-ene-10,3'-indole]-2'-one, which both direct their activity toward SK-VLB. The shared target of these compounds suggests a potential mechanism by which Divaricataester C may influence SK-VLB through the modulation of this enzyme. The evidence indicates that Divaricataester C likely exerts its biological effects by targeting the same enzyme as these other compounds, thereby potentially modulating SK-VLB's function. The integration of these pathways highlights the enzyme as a critical node in the interaction network, underscoring its role in the biological activity of Divaricataester C and its potential therapeutic relevance.",
